page('/literacy/handwriting-practice/','Handwriting practice for kids: trace, write and draw','On-screen handwriting practice for children. Trace letters, write numbers or your name with a finger, stylus or mouse, then save your picture.',crumb([['Story Corner','/literacy/'],['Handwriting practice']])+heading('WRITE · TRACE · DRAW','A little practice, at your pace.','Try together with a grown-up. Use the writing space below, or copy the same prompt into a notebook.')+writingSection+`<div class="wrap"><div class="brand-duo"><div class="brand-art"><img src="${brandBase}kiddo-classroom-ready-to-learn.webp" width="1264" height="1264" alt="A girl in a purple school uniform sits ready at her desk with a book and a pencil, from the Kiddo.school illustration." loading="lazy"></div></div></div><section class="prose wrap"><h2>Start small.</h2><p>Choose one letter or number and practise for a few minutes. Model it slowly, then invite your child to try. Use Undo freely: this is exploration, not a score or a handwriting assessment.</p><h2>Make it comfortable.</h2><p>Rest the device on a stable surface. A fingertip works; a stylus is optional. Try a thicker line and a larger movement if fine movements are difficult. Paper and crayons are always a good alternative. <a href="/downloads/handwriting-practice.svg" download>Download the printable handwriting sheet.</a></p><h2>Keep what you make.</h2><p>Save your page as a PNG image before closing or refreshing. Nothing you draw is sent to us or stored online. Clear and activity changes can be undone during this visit.</p></section>`,{schema:[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:'Handwriting practice',learningResourceType:'Interactive practice',inLanguage:'en'}]});
